    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community of Langley originated during the Reconstruction era as part of an effort to revive the Southern economy through industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/langley_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Langley was named in honor of William C. Langley, a businessman from Brooklyn who was the principal stockholder of the local mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Langley%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town grew around the Langley Cotton Mill, which was originally known as the Kalmia Mill before being expanded in 1870.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/langley_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Langley Pond is a small reservoir located right next to the community that provides a notable local water feature.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/langley_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Langley once featured company-owned housing, schools, and churches designed to attract a family-based workforce for its isolated mill operations.",
